<p>Since the drive back to Maspalomas takes only around 17 minutes, there's rarely a need to plan the day around the transfer itself, but a couple of details are worth bearing in mind if you're coming from Puerto Rico. Because Puerto Rico is built up a hillside, some accommodation blocks have limited direct vehicle access, so it helps to confirm your exact pickup point when booking rather than assuming a driver can pull up right outside every door. This matters more if you're carrying beach or diving equipment picked up during your stay, since a short walk to a more accessible pickup spot is easier to plan for in advance than to work out on the day.</p>
