<p>Puerto Rico is built around Gran Canaria's main marina and functions as the island's principal base for boat trips and watersports, giving it a busy, harbour-facing character. Puerto de Mogán, just along the coast, is a different kind of place entirely — nicknamed the "Little Venice of Gran Canaria" for the small canals and footbridges that thread through its old town, and home to a well-known market held every Friday. Despite the short distance between them, the two resorts feel distinct, which is exactly why so many visitors staying in one choose to spend part of a day in the other.</p>
