<p>Puerto de Mogán, nicknamed the "Little Venice of Gran Canaria" for its canals and footbridges, is a quiet, picturesque harbour town best known for its weekly market held every Friday. Puerto Rico, a short drive along the coast, is a busier, more vertical resort built around Gran Canaria's main marina, and it's where most of the island's boat trips, watersports, and diving excursions are based. The contrast between the two is sharp for such a short distance, which is part of why so many visitors move between them during a single stay.</p>
